WEBVTT

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.670
Just a dream, huh?

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.230
<i>During the recent practice match,</i>

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:43.560
<i>I managed to beat Zakuro-san,
a national-caliber player.</i>

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.270
<i>But it was far from a perfect game.</i>

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.770
<i>I honestly don't know
if I can win if I play her again.</i>

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:59.380
<i>I have to iron out that issue
by the time the training camp ends.</i>

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.910
Training 
Camp!!

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.910
Back 
Home

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.800
<i>If I don't, I'll get destroyed
at the national level.</i>

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.150
<b>Scorching</b>

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.150
<b>Ping Pong Girls</b>

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.800
<b>Eleventh Serve</b>

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.800
<b>Training Camp</b>

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.760
Suzumegahara Municipal Junior High

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.140
Everybody here?

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.060
Yeah!

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.980
Made sure you didn't forget anything?

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.310
Yeah!

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.090
The first-years sure are hyper today.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.620
Let's see if they stay hyper
once we get there.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.730
Is something up with the camp?

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:05.060
Oh, it's your first time, Taily.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.820
You'll see once we get there.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.160
It'll be five days
of nothing but table tennis.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.120
Five days of nothing but table tennis!

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:17.210
Goddamn, there you are!
I looked all over for ya, for Pete's sake!

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:17.920
Oh...

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:26.430
Seriously, I looked all over for you girls.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.390
<i>Kumami...?</i>

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.450
Whoa, it's Kumamin!

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:36.140
Long time no see, Frill Panties.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:38.030
It's been a while, everyone.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.530
What are you doing here?

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.220
I had something to do in the area,
so I dropped by.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.970
I thought it was weird
that you weren't holding morning practice.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.540
But, right, it's time for camp.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.960
It's nice to see the seniors
after so long, too.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.830
Is your ankle fine now, Kiruka-senpai?

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.230
Yeah, completely.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:04.930
And, Munemune-senpai, I see your
powerful boobs are still the same.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.430
Powerful boobs?!

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:08.920
Who is she?

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.080
A friend?

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:13.890
Second-year at Tsubame Girls' Academy,

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:16.040
Tsukinowa Kumami.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.360
She used to be part of our team.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.200
A former teammate?

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.690
She transferred out a bit before you arrived.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:29.870
Or, to be more precise,
she left Suzumegahara for greener pastures.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.580
What do you mean?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.330
Long time no see, A-chan.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:36.820
<i>A-chan?!</i>

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.510
Long time no see.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.420
Who's that? A first-year?

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.840
She transferred in this spring.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:46.720
N-Nice to meet you.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.050
I'm Tsumujikaze Koyori.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.060
<i>I managed to introduce myself all right!</i>

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:53.440
I'm Tsukinowa Kumami.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.020
Hey, A-chan. This girl...

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.560
Kumamin!

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:04.070
It's been ages!
Lemme bunbun your hair buns!

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.570
Bunbun! Bunbun!

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.730
Hey! Get yer filthy hands off of her!

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:12.350
That tickles, ya piece of shit!

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.010
Woohoo!

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:19.560
It's been forever since I've seen
Kumamin's ventriloquy in action!

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.750
It sure is popular.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:25.390
Well, it's the only thing
this washboard has goin' for her.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:28.340
Leave my chest out of it, Kumanosuke-san.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:28.970
Ow.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:33.700
<b>"Ow, ow, don't stretch me!"</b>

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:31.280
Ow, ow!

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:33.260
Don't stretch me!

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.120
Wow!

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.950
It's like the bear really is talking!

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:40.240
Kumamin's ventriloquy is unsurpassed!

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.680
Top class.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.050
The best in Japan!

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.960
You're awesome, Kuma-chan.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.720
It's wonderful!

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:51.270
Y-You're makin' me blush, goddammit!

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.740
So, what'd you come here for?

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:57.790
Surely it wasn't
just to show off your ventriloquy.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.680
That's it, really.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.960
But, well, if I had to say...

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:14.060
I'm here to see you, I guess.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.150
Time to recharge on Vitamin Agari.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:22.880
J-J-Jeez, what's with you?!

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:23.650
Gosh.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:27.050
Y-You came here just for this?

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.880
It's important to me.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:32.110
I haven't seen you in a while,
and I missed you.

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:33.160
What?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:39.420
And here I thought you came
to settle the score from back then.

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:41.600
<i>The score from back then?</i>

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.630
I thought I told you
I won't play you anymore.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.320
And why is that?

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.140
Give me a reason!

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.340
I'm sorry.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.060
Let's get outta here, Kumami!

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.340
Right, they're headed to camp.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:04.750
Let's go.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:06.070
Wait, Kumami!

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:11.680
Have a nice day.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.560
Have a nice...

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.860
Don't you agree, Hokuto?

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:28.340
Wow!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.680
It's so good!

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:43.310
A better practice facility
than our school gym.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.770
An environment where
we can focus on table tennis all day.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.530
We can play until we drop.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.570
I can't wait.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.950
Thanks to the one
who arranged this training camp,

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:58.040
Nipponichi-sensei,
the best teacher in Japan!

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.360
Thank you very much!

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.510
You're the best!

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:06.620
Now, then. The summer tournament
is almost upon us.

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:10.510
And our goal is
to make Nationals, of course.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:14.720
Though, personally,
I'd like to <i>win</i> Nationals.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:20.450
In order to beat the myriad
powerhouse schools and make Nationals,

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:24.620
we'll need to raise our game
by a few levels.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:30.400
The objective of this training camp is
to make us good enough to go to Nationals.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:34.290
We'll train hard to prepare
for the tournament!

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:36.150
Hard!

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.650
<i>Nationals, huh?</i>

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:42.150
<i>There'll be loads of
amazing players like Kururi-san, right?</i>

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:46.460
<i>Just thinking about it
is making my heart race!</i>

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:51.240
Makes your heart race,
doesn't it, Agari-chan?

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:09.310
First Day
Footwork
Serves
Receives
System
Munemune's Boobs Time
Smashes and Blocks

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:09.310
Second Day
Footwork
Multiple Balls
System
In-Game
Free Practice

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.120
Most of the schedule is joint practices.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:05.820
We'll focus on the usual drills today.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:09.310
Uh, one of these items
isn't like the others...

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.760
Starting tomorrow, though,

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.320
there will be two hours of free practice
after joint practice.

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:21.010
The starters are to practice while keeping
the matches from the other day in mind.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:24.180
Especially those who have
identified issues in their game.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:28.500
I want you to iron them out
during this camp.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.690
<i>Was that directed at me?</i>

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.210
<i>Has she noticed my issue?</i>

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.530
Uh, what should we do?

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:40.530
Well, you first-years can review
everything you've learned so far

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:44.350
and work on the areas
you feel you need to improve in.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.570
We'll help with anything
you have trouble with,

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:47.690
so feel free to ask.

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:49.060
Got it!

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:52.320
Shall we begin, then?

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:56.240
Let's make this a productive camp
that is not the least bit boring!

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.450
Let's do this!

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.660
Please.

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:02.290
<i>Agari-chan.</i>

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:05.480
<i>Free practice, huh?</i>

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:07.870
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:10.380
First Day

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:10.380
We'll start with footwork drills.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.330
Fore.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.800
<b>3-Step Shuffle</b>

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:12.800
Middle.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:13.800
Back.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.070
Back.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.220
<b>2-In-1-Out Shuffle</b>

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.360
Pivot.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.220
Fore.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.570
Back.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:21.930
<b>2-In-2-Out Shuffle</b>

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:19.860
Pivot.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:20.610
Fore.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:21.930
Fore.

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:27.140
These drills are all about
getting in the best position to hit.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:29.340
Be deft and quick on your feet.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:31.920
This is both the most basic
and most importance practice,

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.780
so focus!

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:34.650
Right!

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:37.130
Serve Drills

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.590
Receive Drills

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:41.530
System Drills

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:44.240
<b>Munemune's Boobs
 Time</b>

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:44.240
<b>Swing
Check</b>

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:50.460
Whoa!

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.340
Whoa...

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:56.710
Whoa.

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:57.340
Beam!

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:00.850
Let's keep this up!

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.160
Right!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:11.520
Since this is a training camp,
we can focus on practice all day.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:15.350
But is it ever rough.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.110
So this is a training camp...

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.610
I think I might die.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.260
All right, girls.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:23.110
These smash drills are the last for today.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:25.490
Let's end the day on a pleasant note.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.740
Smash practice?!

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:30.150
She's back in action.

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:31.750
So full of life.

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:35.070
Good, good.

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:37.660
You're always great, Koyori-chan.

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:42.780
The practice match has
made your smash even more lethal.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:44.640
Th-Thank you!

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:50.170
The way your boobs bounce
when you smash is picturesque.

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.640
Praise my smash!

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:53.930
Next up, Agari.

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:56.110
Thank you.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:12.250
So boring.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.900
You normally didn't hit
forehand smashes before,

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.170
so I was too surprised
to return it back then.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:24.380
But it's a piece of cake
to deal with now, I suppose.

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:32.350
<i>Agari-chan's smashes</i>

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:34.460
<i>are completely ineffective?</i>

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.320
Hot spring!

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:50.560
No matter how hard practice is, I can get
through it 'cause this is waiting for me!

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:52.840
This is why I love training camp!

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.030
Your love for hot springs
makes you seem like a senior citizen.

00:12:56.030 --> 00:12:59.500
A heated pool would be more exciting.

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.700
Now, now.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:03.550
Don't say that. Let's get in, Hokuto!

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:10.600
Will tomorrow be just as hard?

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.270
We could die.

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:16.520
Wanna go drink some milk?

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.310
Sure!

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:24.070
A-Agari-chan!

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.320
Is something on your mind?

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.200
I-If you're okay with me,

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:32.120
I-I'll gladly hear you out!

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:33.800
Koyori.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:44.760
Not lethal enough?

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:45.860
Yeah.

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:49.440
Right now, my smash
isn't lethal enough to generate winners.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.400
I somehow managed to beat Zakuro-san,

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:56.980
but she returned
my forehand smashes with ease.

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:04.380
As things stand, forget Nationals,

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:07.610
I'm not sure if I can even win
in the district qualifiers.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.380
You're being way too pessimistic.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:12.150
I'm not.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.170
We'll definitely run into Tsubame Academy
in the district qualifiers.

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:19.540
And Kumami's with them this year.

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:22.290
I won't play you anymore.

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.250
I'm sorry.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:34.600
Well, yeah, Kumamin is tough.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.630
Frill is pretty good.

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:40.940
They might be even better than Mozuyama now.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.670
What? Better than Kururi-san's team?

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:44.820
You never know.

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:48.500
I was all excited that I could
hit forehand smashes again,

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:52.880
but all it meant was
that I was finally average.

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:57.890
If I can't finish off rallies,

00:14:57.890 --> 00:14:59.960
I can't compete with players
on powerhouse teams.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:02.710
Huh? You're getting out already, Agari?

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.530
That was quick.

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:06.230
I don't have any time to waste.

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:09.340
I should go to bed early,
practice on my own before joint practice,

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.800
and make every second count.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.840
Then I'll get out, too.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:16.420
Did you soak to your shoulders
and count one hundred?

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:20.450
One hundred?! I haven't...

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:21.760
Then you can't.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.870
Warm yourself fully before you get out.

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:25.280
I sure did.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:28.260
You're always such a stickler for the rules.

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:31.990
Actually, you sound
like an old woman, White Panties.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.410
Seriously, quit referring to people
by the color of their panties!

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:37.690
We have names! Use them!

00:15:39.930 --> 00:15:40.870
Beam.

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:43.270
Peach Panties.

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:44.830
White Panties.

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:45.630
Hanabi.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:48.020
Why does Hanabi get normal treatment?

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.240
Hanabi is Hanabi.

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:52.300
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.270
Fifty-two, fifty-three,
fifty-four, fifty-five...

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:54.320
That's kinda unfair...

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:56.240
You're such a joker, Hokuto.

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:58.390
Fifty-six, fifty-seven,
fifty-eight, fifty-nine...

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:00.980
So, basically,

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:05.680
you want to be able to hit lethal smashes.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.440
Yeah.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:10.240
And do you have a way to do that?

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:14.160
Actually, not at all.

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.110
When you think about it,

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:20.550
you can't make your smash
more lethal overnight.

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:23.380
I want to work something out
during this camp,

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:25.920
but I don't know if I can.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.270
I'll hold them off here!

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:37.400
You go ahead, Hokuto!

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:39.410
Beam, beam...

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.290
Agari-chan?

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:12.260
Can't sleep?

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.650
Koyori?

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:19.800
Agari-chan, if there's
something bothering you, talk to me.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.850
Like I said, my smash...

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:23.940
Is that really all?

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.900
It's Frill, isn't it?

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.640
Oh, Kumamin?

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:31.500
Wha—

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:32.760
Why?

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:33.940
It's plain as day.

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:35.840
Why would it...

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:37.420
Agari-chan.

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:45.930
Tsubame Girls' Academy
isn't just a school for rich girls.

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:47.180
It's also a powerhouse.

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:50.940
Their captain lured Kumami away.

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:52.020
Lured?

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:56.970
She's apparently the only daughter
of the chairman of the board there.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:18:02.100
They say her family runs
loads of table tennis halls.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:05.890
So she recruits players
regardless of their school or grade...

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:09.190
And does whatever she wants,
or so the rumors say.

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:13.860
Well, we don't really
know the details, either.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:16.110
After all, she left so suddenly.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:17.730
I see.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:23.770
You mentioned settling a score from the past
this morning. What was that about?

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:28.050
On the day Kumami left,

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:32.090
I asked her to play me in a farewell match.

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:34.600
But she refused.

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:38.050
We went our separate ways
without ever playing that match.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.060
It wasn't just that match.

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:43.020
About a month before she left,

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:45.280
she stopped playing me in matches.

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:50.830
So I thought that maybe she showed up today

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:55.110
because she felt like playing me now.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:57.280
I mean...

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.170
I mean, you get it, right?

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:01.090
We're table tennis players!

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:04.760
Isn't it only right
to converse using table tennis?

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.830
Isn't it, Koyori?

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:06.930
Y-Yeah!

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:09.350
She's like a hot-blooded gang leader.

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:11.920
Like, "We'll talk with our fists"?

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.290
That's right.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:17.840
If you leave without playing a proper match,
you won't know who's better.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:21.650
I wanted to play her!

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:23.810
So what's her deal?

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:28.380
She wanted to see me,
but she didn't want to play me?

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:31.480
What the heck?

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:34.160
So that's why you've been so on edge.

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:36.680
You get surprisingly hung up
over things, White Panties.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:40.150
Sh-Shut up! I was just
a little bothered by it!

00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:42.610
Is that so?

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:47.180
But, hey, we'll run into Tsubame
in the district qualifiers.

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:50.820
You could just play her then.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:53.280
Well, yeah...

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:57.650
In that case, worrying about Frill now
is a waste of time.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:19:58.710
Waste?

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:02.470
You have to do everything you can right now
to prepare for that match.

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.700
Everything I can do right now?

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.560
Making your smash more lethal.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:11.490
Agari-chan!

00:20:11.490 --> 00:20:14.470
I don't really get the deal with Kumami-san,

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:16.650
but I think I can help with table tennis!

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:21.610
Practice now so you can
feel your heart race with her!

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.760
I'll help!

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:24.860
Okay?

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:27.100
Wh-What are you saying?

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.510
I can figure it out by myself!

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:40.240
W-Well, I wouldn't not say yes
to you helping out a little...

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:42.010
Sure!

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:44.410
Which is it?

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:45.940
It's her usual thing.

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:46.710
Good grief.

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:48.450
What do you mean, good grief?

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:50.980
I guess that's one case closed.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:53.550
All's well that ends well!
Shall we get back to the room?

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:56.190
Yeah. We have an early start tomorrow, too.

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.490
Let's go, Koyori.

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:09.950
Yeah!

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:26.250
Will we practice like yesterday again?

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:29.390
I'm not sure I'll last.

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:36.340
Morning!

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.370
G-Good morning!

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:42.560
Mornin'!

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:44.340
Morning.

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:46.030
Good morning!

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:49.680
Agari-senpai and the rest
sure are up for it!

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:51.240
Yeah. It's amazing.

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:57.140
My, now that's a fine expression.

00:21:57.140 --> 00:21:59.940
I won't be bored today, I take it?

00:23:43.860 --> 00:24:00.000
Preview

00:23:45.170 --> 00:23:47.320
I'll join, too.

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:48.570
You're making me blush, Hokuto!

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:50.750
You can't call this fair use!

00:23:49.520 --> 00:23:51.570
I love table tennis!

00:23:51.020 --> 00:23:53.110
This is my answer!

00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:53.960
This is who I am!

00:23:53.110 --> 00:23:54.760
This is who I am!

00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:57.560
Everyone here really does love table tennis.
